diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket describes a fault that does not exist in the live lab. The sshswitch multilayer switch serving Campus 2 has both VLAN 5 and VLAN 6 SVIs fully operational. The Linux bridge interfaces `br_v5` (10.5.0.254/24) and `br_v6` (10.6.0.254/24) are in UP/LOWER_UP state, carry their correct gateway IP addresses, and are reachable from every end-host tested: pc1, dc_pc5 (both VLAN 5) and pc3, pc4 (VLAN 6) each return 4/4 pings to their respective default gateways with zero packet loss and sub-millisecond latency. The startup script on sshswitch explicitly configures both SVIs with the correct addresses, the running state matches the startup, and FRR/OSPF is advertising both prefixes (10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24) into Area 0 without any omission. The VLAN trunk sub-interfaces (bond0.5, bond0.6, eth0.5, eth0.6) bridged into the respective VLAN bridge domains are also UP, so layer-2 forwarding toward switch4 and its downstream VLAN 5/6 access ports is intact. The premise of the ticket — that SVIs dropped after a reload — is false; no reload or SVI flap has occurred and the gateway interfaces are fully functional. No corrective action is required for the reported symptom.
=== END ===